// ADR 1.10.26h D6: the planted pair's bootstrap side — see the note below.
fn diverge() -> Void { diverge() }

fn main() -> Nat { 0 }

// Both compilers refuse `diverge` with one termination record of one class
// (bootstrap E0062, self-host E0710; both `Elaboration`), so the only thing
// that differs from `planted_selfhost_side.tg` is the blank line above the
// error there: line 2 here, line 3 there. The register expects exactly that
// `LocationsDiffer`; a gate whose location comparison is neutered turns the
// entry Stale. The disk scan skips `planted_*`, so the pair is indexed by name.
